1
00:00:41,437 --> 00:00:48,444
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

2
00:00:56,995 --> 00:00:59,080
2017
PRAGUE

3
00:00:59,164 --> 00:01:01,875
We are at the Prague Harmonie
International Competition finals venue.

4
00:01:01,958 --> 00:01:05,587
Today is the final round,
featuring the two finalists.

5
00:01:05,670 --> 00:01:09,507
Following their exceptional
semifinal performances,

6
00:01:09,591 --> 00:01:12,427
all attention is focused
on today's event.

7
00:01:39,078 --> 00:01:40,079
Let go of me!

8
00:01:40,163 --> 00:01:41,372
I said let go!

9
00:03:04,998 --> 00:03:06,666
Where are we going now?

10
00:03:08,126 --> 00:03:09,294
Excuse me.

11
00:03:09,377 --> 00:03:10,628
Stop, stop!

12
00:03:10,712 --> 00:03:12,380
I want to go to the toilet!

13
00:03:13,965 --> 00:03:15,049
Are you listening to me?

14
00:03:15,133 --> 00:03:17,176
I said I need to go to the restroom!

15
00:03:18,511 --> 00:03:19,345
Cut the crap!

16
00:03:19,929 --> 00:03:22,098
Or else I'll put a bullet
through your head.

17
00:03:54,422 --> 00:03:55,423
Watch it!

18
00:03:55,506 --> 00:03:56,591
No, you watch it.

19
00:03:56,674 --> 00:03:58,092
Don't get blood splatter in the car.

20
00:03:59,385 --> 00:04:02,930
Who do you think you are?
Don't tell me what to do.

21
00:06:04,844 --> 00:06:07,763
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

22
00:06:07,847 --> 00:06:09,432
We will now present

23
00:06:09,515 --> 00:06:11,934
an award to Kang Pi-o…

24
00:06:12,018 --> 00:06:13,186
6 MONTHS AGO

25
00:06:13,269 --> 00:06:15,354
…for bringing honor
to Korea Arts High School.

26
00:06:16,439 --> 00:06:19,817
Kang Pi-o, please come to the podium.

27
00:06:19,901 --> 00:06:21,777
EPISODE 1

28
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:26,240
Is all this necessary?

29
00:06:26,324 --> 00:06:27,575
You performed so much better.

30
00:06:40,421 --> 00:06:41,380
"The above student

31
00:06:41,464 --> 00:06:45,426
is hereby commended
for elevating our school's reputation

32
00:06:45,510 --> 00:06:47,011
by winning the grand prize

33
00:06:47,094 --> 00:06:50,431
at the 27th Lake Erie
International Junior Competition."

34
00:06:57,313 --> 00:06:59,273
CERTIFICATE OF COMMENDATION
NAME: KANG PI-O

35
00:07:05,404 --> 00:07:06,989
DROP OUT, BASTARD
LEAVE, ILLEGITIMATE CHILD

36
00:07:07,073 --> 00:07:08,366
Han-rim, he's over here.

37
00:07:12,912 --> 00:07:15,331
Hey, did you throw this in the trash?

38
00:07:16,624 --> 00:07:18,834
You're so damn full of yourself.

39
00:07:20,002 --> 00:07:23,047
The whole school gathered
for the stupid ceremony

40
00:07:23,130 --> 00:07:25,049
because you won some competition.

41
00:07:25,132 --> 00:07:27,051
You crossed the line, don't you think?

42
00:07:30,805 --> 00:07:31,639
Hey.

43
00:07:31,722 --> 00:07:33,641
Are we just here to make you look good?

44
00:07:34,308 --> 00:07:37,186
Well, I suppose winning a competition

45
00:07:38,020 --> 00:07:41,357
is nothing to Kang Seung-woon's grandson.

46
00:07:42,858 --> 00:07:44,151
You think that's funny?

47
00:07:44,235 --> 00:07:45,444
Let us in on the joke.

48
00:07:49,031 --> 00:07:52,201
Do you think it's my fault
you guys didn't place?

49
00:07:52,868 --> 00:07:54,662
If you're so bitter about not placing,

50
00:07:55,454 --> 00:07:59,667
try to spend less time picking fights
and more time practicing.

51
00:08:01,752 --> 00:08:02,753
Seriously?

52
00:08:04,672 --> 00:08:06,007
What about you?

53
00:08:06,090 --> 00:08:08,426
Aren't you trying to prove yourself

54
00:08:09,176 --> 00:08:11,262
because you're bitter
about your family background?

55
00:08:13,556 --> 00:08:14,974
-Hey!
-What the hell?

56
00:08:15,558 --> 00:08:17,643
What are you guys doing?

57
00:08:18,144 --> 00:08:19,645
-Jeez, it's her again.
-That scared me.

58
00:08:21,647 --> 00:08:24,609
Why are you guys messing with Pi-o again?

59
00:08:24,692 --> 00:08:27,486
Snap out of it, Hong Jae-in.

60
00:08:27,987 --> 00:08:30,406
Stop letting this jerk use you.

61
00:08:32,992 --> 00:08:34,285
Let's go.

62
00:08:34,368 --> 00:08:35,494
Hey, wait up.

63
00:08:41,834 --> 00:08:43,961
Wait, Pi-o!

64
00:08:45,004 --> 00:08:46,964
How many times do I have to tell you?

65
00:08:47,048 --> 00:08:50,051
Try to be just a little more humble.

66
00:08:50,718 --> 00:08:53,304
Those guys are jealous of you as it is.

67
00:08:53,387 --> 00:08:55,514
You didn't have to
throw away that certificate.

68
00:08:55,598 --> 00:08:57,850
Or you could've thrown it away at home.

69
00:08:59,977 --> 00:09:02,730
Why should I have to
cater to everyone else's feelings?

70
00:09:05,983 --> 00:09:07,109
Are you…

71
00:09:08,861 --> 00:09:09,779
a sociopath?

72
00:09:12,531 --> 00:09:14,283
Why don't you tell me what you want?

73
00:09:14,909 --> 00:09:15,785
Me?

74
00:09:16,619 --> 00:09:17,995
I don't want anything.

75
00:09:18,079 --> 00:09:19,872
Oh, yeah? Never mind then.

76
00:09:21,040 --> 00:09:23,626
-Actually, I--
-Sorry.

77
00:09:23,709 --> 00:09:24,835
Find someone else.

78
00:09:24,919 --> 00:09:26,879
You didn't even hear me out.

79
00:09:26,962 --> 00:09:28,923
Weren't you going to ask me
to be your accompanist?

80
00:09:29,757 --> 00:09:30,716
How did you know?

81
00:09:32,677 --> 00:09:34,512
Hey, Pi-o!

82
00:09:34,595 --> 00:09:36,847
Just hear me out.

83
00:09:39,767 --> 00:09:41,185
Pi-o.

84
00:09:42,269 --> 00:09:45,231
I wouldn't ask you if I didn't have to.

85
00:09:45,314 --> 00:09:47,233
But none of the others are any good.

86
00:09:47,858 --> 00:09:50,069
There's no way I can play with them.

87
00:09:50,903 --> 00:09:51,904
I'm busy.

88
00:09:52,530 --> 00:09:54,615
It's not a lot. Just three…

89
00:09:55,408 --> 00:09:56,701
No, wait.

90
00:09:57,576 --> 00:09:58,494
Just twice.

91
00:09:59,161 --> 00:10:03,374
Come on, it won't take up
much of your time.

92
00:10:04,083 --> 00:10:05,126
Hey!

93
00:10:05,209 --> 00:10:08,087
I'm practically begging you here!

94
00:10:13,676 --> 00:10:15,469
I didn't want to say this,

95
00:10:15,553 --> 00:10:17,263
but we're not on the same level.

96
00:10:17,346 --> 00:10:19,098
Playing together
would only expose you.

97
00:10:19,181 --> 00:10:21,016
Why play a concerto like that?

98
00:10:23,269 --> 00:10:25,396
That's a pretty harsh thing to say.

99
00:10:25,980 --> 00:10:27,565
But that's my point.

100
00:10:27,648 --> 00:10:31,360
I'm asking you
to help me out with your skills.

101
00:10:33,404 --> 00:10:35,156
No. I don't want to.

102
00:10:35,239 --> 00:10:37,199
Hey, Kang Pi-o!

103
00:10:41,954 --> 00:10:43,956
Hey, I'm talking to you!

104
00:11:15,863 --> 00:11:16,906
Right.

105
00:11:18,199 --> 00:11:20,284
This is exactly why

106
00:11:20,826 --> 00:11:22,119
I can't lose you.

107
00:11:23,454 --> 00:11:26,499
How do you capture Schumann so perfectly?

108
00:11:47,812 --> 00:11:48,646
Pi-o.

109
00:11:52,650 --> 00:11:54,902
Forget the accompaniment.

110
00:11:55,903 --> 00:11:57,738
Let's just get married.

111
00:11:59,949 --> 00:12:00,825
I seriously need to

112
00:12:02,159 --> 00:12:03,702
listen to you play forever.

113
00:12:10,167 --> 00:12:11,919
Will you just leave already?

114
00:12:12,002 --> 00:12:14,171
Hey, I'm totally serious!

115
00:12:14,255 --> 00:12:17,216
SONGMIN HIGH SCHOOL

116
00:12:40,698 --> 00:12:41,574
Where are you going?

117
00:13:04,013 --> 00:13:05,681
Get up, Choi Jeong-yo!

118
00:13:07,099 --> 00:13:08,267
Everyone, gather around.

119
00:13:12,479 --> 00:13:13,606
I want an answer now.

120
00:13:14,189 --> 00:13:15,858
What will you do
about the music practical?

121
00:13:16,358 --> 00:13:18,944
You really can't play a single instrument?

122
00:13:19,653 --> 00:13:21,196
-Come on, a practical?
-We can't.

123
00:13:21,280 --> 00:13:22,781
I told you a million times.

124
00:13:23,407 --> 00:13:26,160
Bring a triangle or something
and take the practical.

125
00:13:30,289 --> 00:13:31,498
Here's the alternative.

126
00:13:32,499 --> 00:13:35,294
My friend called and said
they need to fill the seats.

127
00:13:35,878 --> 00:13:38,797
If you attend,
I'll give you credit for the practical.

128
00:13:38,881 --> 00:13:39,924
Is that better?

129
00:13:40,007 --> 00:13:41,467
What a shame. I'll pass.

130
00:13:42,134 --> 00:13:43,135
What do you mean?

131
00:13:43,218 --> 00:13:45,554
I'm going out of my way
to cut you some slack.

132
00:13:45,638 --> 00:13:47,222
No one goes to those things anymore.

133
00:13:48,140 --> 00:13:50,017
This is way too much pressure.

134
00:13:50,100 --> 00:13:52,061
Why don't you just give up on us?

135
00:13:52,144 --> 00:13:54,063
-Choi Jeong-yo!
-Here!

136
00:13:58,150 --> 00:13:59,652
I don't want to go.

137
00:14:06,909 --> 00:14:08,243
Hello, Rider Jo!

138
00:14:08,327 --> 00:14:09,578
That idiot.

139
00:14:11,038 --> 00:14:14,500
Man, look at you being responsible
and coming to school every day.

140
00:14:15,584 --> 00:14:16,877
Get into any trouble today?

141
00:14:17,628 --> 00:14:20,130
Want me to get into serious trouble
and get expelled?

142
00:14:20,798 --> 00:14:22,216
You're too chicken to do that.

143
00:14:23,634 --> 00:14:25,970
-Hop on.
-All right, let's go.

144
00:14:34,019 --> 00:14:35,020
Get your fast cash!

145
00:14:35,104 --> 00:14:36,897
NEED CASH FAST?

146
00:14:41,318 --> 00:14:42,486
A real man

147
00:14:43,696 --> 00:14:47,032
never forgets the hard times
he went through.

148
00:14:47,908 --> 00:14:48,784
You boys.

149
00:14:50,327 --> 00:14:52,496
When you make it big someday,

150
00:14:53,080 --> 00:14:54,373
remember me, okay?

151
00:14:54,456 --> 00:14:55,290
Thank you, sir.

152
00:14:57,167 --> 00:14:58,627
-Here.
-Thank you!

153
00:14:58,711 --> 00:15:00,170
You punk.

154
00:15:00,254 --> 00:15:02,006
I gave you a bit extra.

155
00:15:02,089 --> 00:15:03,590
-Here. Work hard.
-Thank you.

156
00:15:03,674 --> 00:15:05,676
-You can all be successful.
-Thank you, sir.

157
00:15:07,511 --> 00:15:09,138
Hey, Jeong-yo.

158
00:15:11,265 --> 00:15:12,725
Eat up, okay?

159
00:15:13,434 --> 00:15:14,852
You've lost weight.

160
00:15:15,686 --> 00:15:16,729
By the way, Jeong-yo,

161
00:15:17,312 --> 00:15:19,940
tell your father to pay up what he owes.

162
00:15:20,024 --> 00:15:21,692
I'm broke as hell right now.

163
00:15:21,775 --> 00:15:24,403
Look at us,
just eating jjajangmyeon every day.

164
00:15:27,031 --> 00:15:28,490
Hello, this is Happy Loan.

165
00:15:28,574 --> 00:15:30,367
-How are you, ma'am?
-Forget it.

166
00:15:30,451 --> 00:15:32,161
-I mean, miss.
-Take it, you punk.

167
00:15:32,244 --> 00:15:34,371
Don't be so stubborn.

168
00:15:34,455 --> 00:15:35,664
Hurry up and eat.

169
00:15:45,632 --> 00:15:47,760
MUSICAL INSTRUMENT ARCADE
TRADITIONAL MARKET

170
00:15:54,224 --> 00:15:57,061
MUSICAL INSTRUMENT ARCADE

171
00:16:25,923 --> 00:16:29,218
I told you to stop bringing me money,
damn it!

172
00:16:30,010 --> 00:16:31,595
It makes it impossible

173
00:16:32,805 --> 00:16:35,516
for me to hate you in peace.

174
00:16:40,938 --> 00:16:41,814
Hey.

175
00:16:42,981 --> 00:16:44,983
Do you feel sorry for me?

176
00:16:45,901 --> 00:16:48,779
Is that why you keep bringing me money?

177
00:16:50,322 --> 00:16:52,199
You're pitiful too.

178
00:16:54,368 --> 00:16:55,702
And so am I.

179
00:16:56,787 --> 00:17:00,290
You're pitiful…

180
00:17:02,751 --> 00:17:04,920
and I'm pitiful too.

181
00:17:19,726 --> 00:17:22,312
GRAND PRIZE
PIANO, CHOI JEONG-YO

182
00:17:47,171 --> 00:17:49,464
NOTICE OF OVERDUE HEALTH INSURANCE PREMIUM

183
00:17:49,548 --> 00:17:52,217
NOTICE OF OVERDUE INTEREST

184
00:18:06,815 --> 00:18:08,192
-Hello.
-Hey.

185
00:18:09,651 --> 00:18:11,528
-Taking good care of yourself?
-Yes, ma'am.

186
00:19:16,176 --> 00:19:19,805
It feels amazing
to finally watch a proper performance.

187
00:19:21,014 --> 00:19:23,934
How is Hyun-soo still so good
after all this time?

188
00:19:24,017 --> 00:19:25,435
Most people lose their touch

189
00:19:25,519 --> 00:19:28,480
and just go through the motions
when they hit middle age.

190
00:19:29,856 --> 00:19:33,277
Maestro Kang made it so obvious
he was fond of Hyun-soo.

191
00:19:33,860 --> 00:19:37,239
He won't even shake hands
if he doesn't like a performance.

192
00:19:38,031 --> 00:19:41,994
A conductor shouldn't be
so transparent with his emotions.

193
00:19:42,077 --> 00:19:43,745
It intimidates the people he works with.

194
00:19:46,081 --> 00:19:48,583
Yes, I suppose you're right.

195
00:19:50,252 --> 00:19:52,587
Did you find an orchestra
for the concerto?

196
00:19:52,671 --> 00:19:54,381
Oh, I have meetings next week

197
00:19:54,464 --> 00:19:57,676
with the Gyeongseong Philharmonic
and the Seonghan Philharmonic.

198
00:19:58,802 --> 00:20:00,512
Don't worry about a thing.

199
00:20:00,595 --> 00:20:03,432
It's Pi-o. Who would turn him down?

200
00:20:03,515 --> 00:20:06,518
I know you're busy
trying to win Hyun-soo over,

201
00:20:07,352 --> 00:20:10,689
but if you neglect my son because of it,
I'll terminate our contract.

202
00:20:12,441 --> 00:20:15,444
Come on. I wouldn't do that.

203
00:20:16,028 --> 00:20:19,156
The entire company is focused on him.

204
00:20:21,700 --> 00:20:25,329
By the way, Jae-in said
you refused to be her accompanist.

205
00:20:26,955 --> 00:20:27,998
I'm sorry.

206
00:20:29,207 --> 00:20:31,126
Don't worry about it.
You made the right call.

207
00:20:31,668 --> 00:20:35,422
Honestly, it'd benefit me more
if you spent that time practicing

208
00:20:35,505 --> 00:20:37,007
than helping that brat out.

209
00:20:38,592 --> 00:20:41,094
And I don't want your mom
to come after me.

210
00:20:44,639 --> 00:20:46,266
I'd love to stay here.

211
00:20:46,933 --> 00:20:49,353
Performing with you today made me realize

212
00:20:49,436 --> 00:20:52,773
what a privilege it is to play with you.

213
00:20:52,856 --> 00:20:54,941
Not at all, sir. You're too kind.

214
00:20:58,904 --> 00:20:59,905
You're home.

215
00:21:05,744 --> 00:21:06,578
Hey, you're here.

216
00:21:09,289 --> 00:21:12,584
Mr. Kang felt it was too early
to call it a night, so…

217
00:21:13,377 --> 00:21:16,129
I enjoyed your performance today.

218
00:21:17,297 --> 00:21:18,131
Thanks.

219
00:21:18,215 --> 00:21:20,217
I heard Hyun-jeong's company
made you an offer.

220
00:21:20,300 --> 00:21:22,677
Yes, I've decided to stay
in Korea for a while.

221
00:21:23,929 --> 00:21:26,556
You've probably had dinner already,
so join us for a drink.

222
00:21:26,640 --> 00:21:27,641
No, thank you.

223
00:21:31,978 --> 00:21:33,313
You must be Pi-o.

224
00:21:37,234 --> 00:21:38,735
I've heard a lot about you.

225
00:21:38,819 --> 00:21:40,237
You took first place at Lake Erie?

226
00:21:43,073 --> 00:21:44,825
As expected of your grandson, sir.

227
00:21:44,908 --> 00:21:47,494
He must've inherited your musical talent.

228
00:21:47,577 --> 00:21:48,995
Stop talking nonsense.

229
00:21:50,038 --> 00:21:54,167
Don't give a talentless kid false hope,
and be careful with your praise.

230
00:21:54,918 --> 00:21:58,213
Empty praise does more harm than good.

231
00:21:59,089 --> 00:22:00,382
-Father.
-Go upstairs.

232
00:22:01,758 --> 00:22:03,969
I don't want to ruin my night.

233
00:22:17,858 --> 00:22:21,319
How could you say that
in front of Hyun-soo?

234
00:22:21,403 --> 00:22:23,280
You can hate me all you want!

235
00:22:23,363 --> 00:22:25,615
But why say things like that
with Pi-o right there?

236
00:22:25,699 --> 00:22:29,703
Don't expect me to live through your child
the way you do.

237
00:22:29,786 --> 00:22:33,248
But he's still your grandson,
and he's my son!

238
00:22:33,331 --> 00:22:34,458
Don't fool yourself.

239
00:22:35,333 --> 00:22:38,128
The only reason I let you two live here

240
00:22:38,211 --> 00:22:41,173
is out of pity for you
trying to play mother,

241
00:22:41,256 --> 00:22:43,049
not because I accept him as my grandson.

242
00:22:43,133 --> 00:22:45,469
Why can't you accept him? Why?

243
00:22:45,552 --> 00:22:48,805
You expect me to accept a kid
with no known father as my grandson?

244
00:22:50,056 --> 00:22:53,268
But more than that,
he doesn't have what it takes.

245
00:22:53,351 --> 00:22:55,770
Stop wasting your time
on that hopeless fool

246
00:22:55,854 --> 00:22:57,689
and focus on your own life!

247
00:22:58,815 --> 00:22:59,816
Father!

248
00:23:07,324 --> 00:23:08,325
Start playing.

249
00:23:38,855 --> 00:23:41,858
Hail, Mary, full of grace,
the Lord is with thee.

250
00:23:43,193 --> 00:23:46,446
Blessed art thou amongst women,

251
00:23:46,530 --> 00:23:48,865
and blessed is
the fruit of thy womb, Jesus.

252
00:23:50,492 --> 00:23:52,244
Holy Mary, Mother of God,

253
00:23:53,036 --> 00:23:54,621
pray for us sinners,

254
00:23:55,372 --> 00:23:57,374
now and at the hour of our death.

255
00:23:58,291 --> 00:23:59,209
Amen.

256
00:24:02,587 --> 00:24:04,005
Holy Mary, Mother of God,

257
00:24:05,006 --> 00:24:06,841
pray for us sinners,

258
00:24:08,468 --> 00:24:10,387
now and at the hour of our death.

259
00:24:11,221 --> 00:24:12,389
Amen.

260
00:24:12,472 --> 00:24:14,432
Holy Mary, Mother of God,

261
00:24:15,684 --> 00:24:17,519
pray for us sinners,

262
00:24:18,770 --> 00:24:21,231
now and at the hour of our death.

263
00:24:22,274 --> 00:24:23,191
Amen.

264
00:24:25,944 --> 00:24:26,778
Come in.

265
00:24:40,292 --> 00:24:42,335
I have something to tell you.

266
00:24:43,587 --> 00:24:46,715
Do you really think
I don't have what it takes?

267
00:24:47,465 --> 00:24:50,468
Or do you just want to think that
because you hate me?

268
00:24:52,554 --> 00:24:55,056
I've looked up to you since I was little.

269
00:24:56,099 --> 00:24:59,519
I gave it everything I had
just to earn one compliment from you.

270
00:25:00,395 --> 00:25:03,064
But even after I took first place
in so many competitions,

271
00:25:03,148 --> 00:25:05,483
you never once glanced at me.

272
00:25:06,192 --> 00:25:07,944
If it's because you hate me--

273
00:25:08,028 --> 00:25:09,446
So you're asking…

274
00:25:14,284 --> 00:25:18,830
why I'd put down a talented kid like you
just because of my personal feelings.

275
00:25:21,207 --> 00:25:22,083
Is that it?

276
00:25:56,660 --> 00:25:57,994
What do you think you're doing?

277
00:26:02,707 --> 00:26:05,001
You think I care to see you
show off your technique?

278
00:26:56,678 --> 00:26:59,848
You have the nerve to complain
about fairness with skills like this?

279
00:27:01,349 --> 00:27:05,145
With a performance
full of nothing but hollow desire?

280
00:27:08,064 --> 00:27:11,067
The people I despise the most in the world

281
00:27:11,151 --> 00:27:13,278
are those who mistake
the greatness of their music

282
00:27:13,820 --> 00:27:16,656
for proof that they themselves are great.

283
00:27:17,407 --> 00:27:18,450
Unfortunately,

284
00:27:20,326 --> 00:27:21,494
you're one of them.

285
00:27:25,248 --> 00:27:26,833
I've never thought of myself that way!

286
00:27:27,417 --> 00:27:29,502
All I wanted was your approval.

287
00:27:29,586 --> 00:27:31,254
Is that so wrong?

288
00:27:35,884 --> 00:27:36,801
Just once.

289
00:27:37,802 --> 00:27:39,429
Give me one more chance.

290
00:27:40,221 --> 00:27:42,724
If you still say no
after I play for you again,

291
00:27:44,225 --> 00:27:45,894
I'll quit playing the piano.

292
00:27:45,977 --> 00:27:47,771
I don't have time to spare for you.

293
00:27:48,271 --> 00:27:49,856
Even for the Noblesse Classical Concert?

294
00:27:52,066 --> 00:27:53,526
You arrogant fool.

295
00:27:54,778 --> 00:27:58,114
Winning a few competitions
has made you laughably arrogant.

296
00:28:01,993 --> 00:28:03,119
What if I do get to play there?

297
00:28:04,621 --> 00:28:06,039
Will you come watch me perform?

298
00:28:06,915 --> 00:28:07,957
Fine.

299
00:28:08,541 --> 00:28:10,502
Let's see you try.

300
00:28:10,585 --> 00:28:13,546
But if I still feel the same way then…

301
00:28:15,548 --> 00:28:18,051
you'll need to take responsibility
for what you said.

302
00:28:26,100 --> 00:28:27,352
That's absurd.

303
00:28:29,312 --> 00:28:31,606
You can't change teachers
right before the competition.

304
00:28:32,524 --> 00:28:35,109
You know how important it is
to get into Professor Seo's inner circle.

305
00:28:35,193 --> 00:28:37,529
That's not important to me.

306
00:28:37,612 --> 00:28:39,656
I need a real teacher

307
00:28:40,740 --> 00:28:42,075
who can teach me properly.

308
00:28:42,158 --> 00:28:43,159
How could that…

309
00:28:45,578 --> 00:28:47,205
How could that not be important?

310
00:28:47,288 --> 00:28:49,207
It all comes down to business in the end.

311
00:28:50,834 --> 00:28:54,128
And of all people,
why does it have to be Hyun-soo?

312
00:28:55,380 --> 00:28:58,883
He has exceptional talent,
but he's still only a performer.

313
00:28:59,801 --> 00:29:01,427
I told Grandfather

314
00:29:01,511 --> 00:29:04,138
that he'd see me perform
at the Noblesse Classical Concert.

315
00:29:05,265 --> 00:29:08,434
And I told him I'd quit the piano
if he still didn't approve.

316
00:29:08,518 --> 00:29:09,894
Do you really think Professor Seo

317
00:29:10,895 --> 00:29:12,105
could pull that off?

318
00:29:12,188 --> 00:29:14,274
Why did you say that
without talking to me…

319
00:29:14,858 --> 00:29:15,900
Pi-o!

320
00:29:18,736 --> 00:29:19,654
Are you off to school?

321
00:29:27,203 --> 00:29:28,079
Have a good day.

322
00:29:36,754 --> 00:29:38,381
I have to say, Pi-o is smart.

323
00:29:39,173 --> 00:29:42,051
He knows exactly what he needs.

324
00:29:44,637 --> 00:29:47,265
You talk like
it doesn't concern you at all.

325
00:29:50,435 --> 00:29:51,936
Why are you being so hostile?

326
00:29:53,104 --> 00:29:54,147
Let's be honest.

327
00:29:54,939 --> 00:29:58,443
Everyone in the music industry knows
Professor Seo is overrated.

328
00:30:00,236 --> 00:30:03,114
I think Pi-o made the right call.

329
00:30:03,990 --> 00:30:05,700
If only Father had supported him,

330
00:30:05,783 --> 00:30:08,286
he wouldn't have had to
turn to Professor Seo.

331
00:30:09,954 --> 00:30:13,041
How could you possibly know what it's like
to be completely powerless, Mother?

332
00:30:56,668 --> 00:30:58,169
You're really good.

333
00:30:58,920 --> 00:31:00,922
I can't find a single flaw.

334
00:31:01,673 --> 00:31:03,299
Why did you come to me?

335
00:31:03,383 --> 00:31:04,717
You don't need my help.

336
00:31:05,635 --> 00:31:06,803
That's not true.

337
00:31:08,888 --> 00:31:11,140
You didn't like how I played.

338
00:31:13,017 --> 00:31:14,435
That isn't true.

339
00:31:17,021 --> 00:31:20,692
You should just learn from Professor Seo.

340
00:31:30,118 --> 00:31:31,327
What did he say?

341
00:31:54,434 --> 00:31:57,061
You should just learn from Professor Seo.

342
00:31:59,355 --> 00:32:02,734
You have the nerve to complain
about fairness with skills like this?

343
00:32:03,776 --> 00:32:07,447
With a performance
full of nothing but hollow desire?

344
00:32:12,785 --> 00:32:15,747
ARTS & MUSIC HALL

345
00:32:41,147 --> 00:32:42,315
Man, I'm dying here.

346
00:32:44,942 --> 00:32:46,527
I can't listen to this anymore.

347
00:32:47,653 --> 00:32:49,530
-Let's go.
-All right.

348
00:32:50,406 --> 00:32:52,742
-Hurry up before the teacher sees us.
-Okay.

349
00:32:54,285 --> 00:32:55,536
Let's go.

350
00:33:11,969 --> 00:33:13,304
Come on, Jeong-yo. Let's go.

351
00:33:14,680 --> 00:33:15,890
You guys go ahead.

352
00:33:48,172 --> 00:33:49,882
KANG PI-O (17 YEARS OLD)
KOREA ARTS HIGH SCHOOL

353
00:33:50,967 --> 00:33:51,926
Kang Pi-o?

354
00:33:55,596 --> 00:33:58,641
Hey, do you have an extra handkerchief?

355
00:34:00,726 --> 00:34:03,020
What's your name?

356
00:34:03,104 --> 00:34:04,438
Kang Pi-o.

357
00:34:33,301 --> 00:34:34,218
KANG PI-O
1ST PRIZE

358
00:34:34,302 --> 00:34:35,803
Look over here, please!

359
00:34:35,887 --> 00:34:38,139
-Pi-o!
-Over here!

360
00:34:38,222 --> 00:34:39,473
Can we get a photo?

361
00:34:39,557 --> 00:34:41,434
They know how amazing you are, don't they?

362
00:34:41,517 --> 00:34:43,227
-Look over here!
-Please, Pi-o!

363
00:34:44,145 --> 00:34:45,897
Why are you so upset?

364
00:34:46,647 --> 00:34:49,442
Kang Pi-o, the perfectionist.

365
00:34:50,735 --> 00:34:52,153
What didn't you like?

366
00:34:53,070 --> 00:34:54,280
My cadenza was a disaster.

367
00:34:54,363 --> 00:34:56,824
CADENZA: A VIRTUOSIC, IMPROVISED SOLO
NEAR THE END OF A CONCERTO MOVEMENT

368
00:34:56,908 --> 00:34:58,451
It wasn't like that during practice.

369
00:35:00,953 --> 00:35:03,623
You know, I've been thinking.

370
00:35:04,582 --> 00:35:07,043
Overdoing it in the cadenza

371
00:35:07,752 --> 00:35:09,253
is a bit tacky.

372
00:35:09,337 --> 00:35:10,796
Playing it with a lighter touch

373
00:35:11,380 --> 00:35:13,633
actually blended better
with the orchestra today.

374
00:35:14,634 --> 00:35:17,220
A pianist shouldn't
race ahead of the music, right?

375
00:35:24,143 --> 00:35:25,561
-Hey, Pi-o!
-Pi-o!

376
00:35:25,645 --> 00:35:27,563
-Hello, ma'am.
-Get in, kids.

377
00:35:28,231 --> 00:35:30,107
I left my sheet music in the waiting room.

378
00:35:30,191 --> 00:35:31,567
Go get it.

379
00:35:34,779 --> 00:35:35,905
Wait for me.

380
00:35:37,114 --> 00:35:39,283
5TH CHEONGUN
INTERNATIONAL MUSIC COMPETITION

381
00:35:41,786 --> 00:35:43,246
Are you sure you can cut class like this?

382
00:35:43,913 --> 00:35:45,081
Your teacher won't say anything?

383
00:35:46,165 --> 00:35:50,503
My future husband's
military exemption is on the line.

384
00:35:51,212 --> 00:35:52,213
You think class matters?

385
00:35:53,130 --> 00:35:53,965
Cut it out.

386
00:36:00,054 --> 00:36:00,888
Who's that?

387
00:36:02,181 --> 00:36:03,516
Who's playing so well?

388
00:36:09,939 --> 00:36:10,856
Damn it.

389
00:36:10,940 --> 00:36:12,692
Hey, Pi-o.

390
00:36:13,943 --> 00:36:15,903
Find out who that is.

391
00:36:16,821 --> 00:36:17,947
Hello, teacher.

392
00:36:18,656 --> 00:36:20,032
I caught a cold.

393
00:36:25,079 --> 00:36:27,707
KANG PI-O

394
00:36:46,684 --> 00:36:47,893
Who are you?

395
00:36:47,977 --> 00:36:50,354
Who the hell are you,
looking at my sheet music like that?

396
00:36:51,981 --> 00:36:52,857
I'm sorry.

397
00:36:54,108 --> 00:36:55,568
I didn't mean to.

398
00:36:57,695 --> 00:36:58,529
Hey.

399
00:37:00,865 --> 00:37:03,034
Don't you remember me?

400
00:37:03,743 --> 00:37:05,161
Who are you?

401
00:37:07,413 --> 00:37:09,373
Never mind. I'm sorry.

402
00:37:10,207 --> 00:37:12,376
By the way,
your cadenza sounded a bit dry.

403
00:37:12,460 --> 00:37:13,711
Was that intentional?

404
00:37:20,301 --> 00:37:21,469
I just…

405
00:37:22,970 --> 00:37:25,765
That's just what I thought.

406
00:37:31,729 --> 00:37:33,022
Critique me however you want.

407
00:37:33,105 --> 00:37:34,732
But if you're such an expert,

408
00:37:35,733 --> 00:37:38,110
why don't you get up on stage
instead of running your mouth?

409
00:37:42,990 --> 00:37:45,242
Was that you playing just now?

410
00:37:47,036 --> 00:37:48,537
That's amazing.

411
00:37:49,246 --> 00:37:51,916
Hey, you were really good.

412
00:37:53,000 --> 00:37:54,168
What school do you go to?

413
00:37:54,251 --> 00:37:55,669
Seonye? Deokmyeong?

414
00:37:57,880 --> 00:37:59,924
Hey, hold on.

415
00:38:00,007 --> 00:38:00,883
Wait a minute!

416
00:38:03,761 --> 00:38:05,054
"Songmin"?

417
00:38:05,721 --> 00:38:07,056
That's not an arts high school.

418
00:38:09,934 --> 00:38:11,394
This is even more amazing.

419
00:38:12,603 --> 00:38:16,273
Hey, can I get your number?

420
00:38:17,024 --> 00:38:19,777
-You see, I play the viola--
-Leave me alone.

421
00:38:20,903 --> 00:38:21,779
Hey!

422
00:39:08,617 --> 00:39:10,995
By the way,
your cadenza sounded a bit dry.

423
00:39:11,078 --> 00:39:12,121
Was that intentional?

424
00:39:21,714 --> 00:39:23,048
KANG PI-O
1ST PRIZE

425
00:39:23,966 --> 00:39:26,427
MUSICAL INSTRUMENT STREET

426
00:39:53,329 --> 00:39:55,498
Hey, why aren't you playing?

427
00:39:55,581 --> 00:39:57,750
Ma'am, the thing is…

428
00:39:58,334 --> 00:40:00,711
The way you play is a bit emotionless.

429
00:40:02,046 --> 00:40:04,381
Can you put some life into it?

430
00:40:04,465 --> 00:40:07,885
The notes sound flat and lifeless to me.

431
00:40:07,968 --> 00:40:09,011
What are you saying?

432
00:40:09,470 --> 00:40:10,846
Focus on your own playing.

433
00:40:10,930 --> 00:40:13,766
I know I'm not good.

434
00:40:14,642 --> 00:40:16,727
That's why if you don't play well,

435
00:40:17,978 --> 00:40:19,355
we're both doomed.

436
00:40:21,607 --> 00:40:24,109
If you're so dissatisfied,
find another accompanist.

437
00:40:26,487 --> 00:40:28,739
Wait, ma'am. That's not what I meant.

438
00:40:29,365 --> 00:40:30,199
Ma'am?

439
00:40:31,617 --> 00:40:32,493
Ma'am!

440
00:40:47,424 --> 00:40:50,261
SONGMIN HIGH SCHOOL

441
00:40:54,181 --> 00:40:55,099
She's pretty.

442
00:41:01,564 --> 00:41:02,398
Jeez!

443
00:41:03,148 --> 00:41:04,650
-Lucky you, man.
-Leave.

444
00:41:04,733 --> 00:41:05,943
Who are you?

445
00:41:06,026 --> 00:41:06,902
Oh my.

446
00:41:07,736 --> 00:41:09,363
You don't remember me?

447
00:41:09,446 --> 00:41:11,782
We met at the music hall.

448
00:41:13,450 --> 00:41:14,910
What is she talking about?

449
00:41:14,994 --> 00:41:18,080
I was totally blown away
when I heard you play.

450
00:41:18,163 --> 00:41:20,541
And I'm looking for an accompanist.

451
00:41:21,041 --> 00:41:23,043
So can you please do it?

452
00:41:23,127 --> 00:41:24,336
Get lost.

453
00:41:24,420 --> 00:41:26,755
Seriously? You didn't even hear the offer.

454
00:41:27,548 --> 00:41:30,843
I'll pay you really well
for the accompaniment.

455
00:41:31,969 --> 00:41:33,304
I said get lost.

456
00:41:33,387 --> 00:41:35,222
Okay, then how about this?

457
00:41:38,225 --> 00:41:39,184
My mom

458
00:41:39,810 --> 00:41:42,438
is the head of a classical music agency.

459
00:41:43,230 --> 00:41:45,983
I'll talk to her and get you an audition.

460
00:41:46,066 --> 00:41:47,943
The way I see it, you're a genius.

461
00:41:48,027 --> 00:41:50,362
Are you going to let your genius
go to waste like this?

462
00:41:50,863 --> 00:41:53,824
Genius, my foot. Go be a genius yourself.

463
00:41:54,742 --> 00:41:56,410
I don't need that nonsense.

464
00:41:59,288 --> 00:42:00,247
A million won!

465
00:42:08,047 --> 00:42:08,964
Don't tell me

466
00:42:10,299 --> 00:42:11,884
you thought I'd pay you peanuts?

467
00:42:12,760 --> 00:42:14,386
Of course not.

468
00:42:15,429 --> 00:42:19,183
Normally, I pay 100,000 won per session.

469
00:42:19,892 --> 00:42:21,101
But since you're special,

470
00:42:21,894 --> 00:42:22,895
I'll pay you 200,000 won.

471
00:42:22,978 --> 00:42:25,397
So five sessions would earn you…

472
00:42:27,483 --> 00:42:28,484
a million won.

473
00:42:29,526 --> 00:42:31,195
Sounds like a really good gig, right?

474
00:42:33,072 --> 00:42:34,698
You arrogant punk!

475
00:42:36,450 --> 00:42:37,284
So tell me.

476
00:42:38,619 --> 00:42:40,579
What's wrong with my teaching?

477
00:42:40,663 --> 00:42:42,122
What's the problem?

478
00:42:43,165 --> 00:42:47,044
I'm running an entrance exam business
and don't care about music, is that it?

479
00:42:47,753 --> 00:42:50,089
Tell me the truth. Who is it?

480
00:42:50,172 --> 00:42:51,882
You want to switch to another professor,

481
00:42:51,965 --> 00:42:54,593
but you feel bad leaving,
so you're trying to blame me, right?

482
00:42:55,302 --> 00:42:56,470
It's not like that, sir.

483
00:42:57,221 --> 00:42:59,973
Oh, come on. "It's not like that"?

484
00:43:00,891 --> 00:43:03,352
Like hell it isn't.

485
00:43:06,021 --> 00:43:08,357
I don't think it's right,

486
00:43:08,440 --> 00:43:11,777
but you keep telling me
to follow your playing technique!

487
00:43:11,860 --> 00:43:14,154
I'll just end up a carbon copy of you!

488
00:43:14,238 --> 00:43:15,239
What?

489
00:43:17,282 --> 00:43:18,659
Damn it.

490
00:43:19,702 --> 00:43:20,577
Get out.

491
00:43:21,328 --> 00:43:22,663
I never want to see you again.

492
00:43:23,664 --> 00:43:26,083
I'm going to do everything in my power

493
00:43:26,166 --> 00:43:28,669
to get you blacklisted
in the music industry.

494
00:43:28,752 --> 00:43:30,170
Now get out.

495
00:43:30,254 --> 00:43:31,088
Get out!

496
00:43:48,689 --> 00:43:49,898
Hey, Choi Jeong-yo!

497
00:43:51,275 --> 00:43:52,151
Let's go.

498
00:44:04,913 --> 00:44:06,165
You practiced, right?

499
00:44:09,209 --> 00:44:10,794
Let's hear you play.

500
00:44:11,545 --> 00:44:12,463
Pay me first.

501
00:44:13,630 --> 00:44:15,007
You're something else.

502
00:44:19,762 --> 00:44:20,596
Here.

503
00:44:21,597 --> 00:44:23,682
I'll give you the rest afterward.

504
00:44:23,766 --> 00:44:24,850
That's okay, right?

505
00:44:29,229 --> 00:44:30,105
Go ahead then.

506
00:45:26,620 --> 00:45:28,580
-Get home safely.
-Okay.

507
00:45:29,248 --> 00:45:30,707
And give some serious thought

508
00:45:31,834 --> 00:45:36,630
to serving on the gifted school
audition panel, all right?

509
00:45:36,713 --> 00:45:37,923
I'll do that.

510
00:45:38,924 --> 00:45:40,592
I wonder who we'll get this year.

511
00:45:41,093 --> 00:45:43,011
We had many violinists last year…

512
00:45:44,429 --> 00:45:45,347
What is it?

513
00:46:20,382 --> 00:46:21,300
Who are you?

514
00:46:22,801 --> 00:46:23,969
What school do you attend?

515
00:46:24,970 --> 00:46:26,638
He's from another school.

516
00:46:26,722 --> 00:46:29,182
I just brought him as my accompanist.

517
00:46:30,392 --> 00:46:31,226
Is that so?

518
00:46:37,316 --> 00:46:38,358
Wait.

519
00:46:38,942 --> 00:46:40,110
Hey, stop right there!

520
00:46:42,738 --> 00:46:43,906
Wait a minute!

521
00:46:46,033 --> 00:46:49,036
Let go of me!
I just came here for the gig!

522
00:46:51,830 --> 00:46:54,416
I want my money first. It's 100,000 won.

523
00:46:58,712 --> 00:46:59,755
Here you go.

524
00:47:00,714 --> 00:47:01,965
Play the piece from earlier.

525
00:47:18,440 --> 00:47:19,733
Can you try modulating?

526
00:47:33,956 --> 00:47:35,499
Okay. Can you try a variation next?

527
00:48:19,084 --> 00:48:20,460
What's your name?

528
00:48:23,213 --> 00:48:24,047
Choi Jeong-yo.

529
00:48:25,716 --> 00:48:26,675
Jeong-yo.

530
00:48:27,592 --> 00:48:29,428
Where are you taking piano lessons?

531
00:48:29,511 --> 00:48:31,430
-I'm not taking any.
-What?

532
00:48:32,055 --> 00:48:34,391
I just play the piano at home
when I'm bored.

533
00:48:36,852 --> 00:48:37,686
Why don't you

534
00:48:38,395 --> 00:48:40,480
enroll here and get some proper training?

535
00:48:49,281 --> 00:48:51,033
So that's why you wanted to see me.

536
00:48:55,620 --> 00:48:57,914
I'm sorry, but I'm not that stupid.

537
00:48:57,998 --> 00:48:59,166
What do you mean?

538
00:48:59,249 --> 00:49:01,793
You're trying to recruit students
and shake them down.

539
00:49:01,877 --> 00:49:02,961
I don't have any money.

540
00:49:04,129 --> 00:49:04,963
Goodbye.

541
00:49:06,548 --> 00:49:07,382
That's not true.

542
00:49:08,425 --> 00:49:09,634
If you want,

543
00:49:09,718 --> 00:49:11,845
we can provide everything,
including a dorm room.

544
00:49:12,596 --> 00:49:14,890
Our school has a scholarship program
for gifted students.

545
00:49:15,640 --> 00:49:17,642
Forget about tuition or lesson fees.

546
00:49:17,726 --> 00:49:19,686
You'd just have to focus on
playing the piano.

547
00:49:20,270 --> 00:49:21,605
And after that?

548
00:49:22,314 --> 00:49:24,274
How would I make a living as a pianist?

549
00:49:25,525 --> 00:49:27,110
I mean, people like you

550
00:49:28,028 --> 00:49:31,490
have a lot of money,
so you can afford to be artists, but me?

551
00:49:32,157 --> 00:49:33,492
Man…

552
00:49:35,410 --> 00:49:37,037
I'll starve to death as a pianist.

553
00:49:38,121 --> 00:49:39,247
Have a nice day.

554
00:49:40,207 --> 00:49:41,124
Wait a minute.

555
00:49:42,584 --> 00:49:45,378
Call me if you ever change your mind.

556
00:49:51,676 --> 00:49:52,761
As far as I can tell,

557
00:49:53,470 --> 00:49:55,472
you've got nothing to worry about.

558
00:49:57,057 --> 00:49:58,850
Reach out to me whenever.

559
00:49:59,559 --> 00:50:00,477
Okay?

560
00:50:00,977 --> 00:50:01,937
Sure.

561
00:50:03,480 --> 00:50:04,397
Goodbye.

562
00:50:19,663 --> 00:50:20,705
What just happened?

563
00:50:21,289 --> 00:50:24,251
Did the director
just offer you a scholarship?

564
00:50:25,877 --> 00:50:27,379
That's crazy!

565
00:50:28,338 --> 00:50:29,798
See?

566
00:50:29,881 --> 00:50:32,467
I told you that you're a genius.

567
00:50:33,218 --> 00:50:36,555
I knew it. My intuition is never wrong.

568
00:50:38,056 --> 00:50:40,433
So? You're going to transfer here, right?

569
00:50:41,309 --> 00:50:42,435
No.

570
00:50:42,519 --> 00:50:43,979
What? Are you insane?

571
00:50:45,564 --> 00:50:46,773
Trust me,

572
00:50:46,857 --> 00:50:49,192
people are desperate
to get into this school.

573
00:50:49,693 --> 00:50:52,445
Pull yourself together
and think this through.

574
00:50:52,529 --> 00:50:54,698
This is a rare opportunity.

575
00:50:55,282 --> 00:50:56,616
I don't want to.

576
00:50:56,700 --> 00:50:57,951
Seriously?

577
00:50:58,034 --> 00:50:59,870
Why not? Give me a reason.

578
00:50:59,953 --> 00:51:02,122
I don't know. I just don't want to.

579
00:51:02,873 --> 00:51:04,958
Why are you making a fuss?
Are you in on this too?

580
00:51:11,965 --> 00:51:13,842
Who on earth is that kid?

581
00:51:15,510 --> 00:51:19,181
It's not refined yet,
but his raw talent is exceptional.

582
00:51:19,806 --> 00:51:22,851
I haven't heard anyone
play like that before.

583
00:51:24,060 --> 00:51:25,562
But still,

584
00:51:25,645 --> 00:51:27,856
what made you suggest
he transfer right away?

585
00:51:29,941 --> 00:51:31,443
It was about seven years ago.

586
00:51:31,526 --> 00:51:34,613
I went to judge a competition,
and I saw this kid.

587
00:51:34,696 --> 00:51:37,866
For some reason,
I just couldn't forget his performance.

588
00:51:37,949 --> 00:51:41,161
I've regretted letting him go ever since.

589
00:51:41,745 --> 00:51:43,914
And that kid's name was

590
00:51:44,623 --> 00:51:45,999
Choi Jeong-yo.

591
00:51:50,003 --> 00:51:51,838
Dude, help me choose between these.

592
00:51:51,922 --> 00:51:56,092
NEED CASH FAST?

593
00:51:59,554 --> 00:52:02,515
KOREA ARTS HIGH SCHOOL
DIRECTOR YOON SEON-JU

594
00:52:06,228 --> 00:52:09,898
Why don't you enroll here
and get some proper training?

595
00:52:38,385 --> 00:52:39,261
Is that you, Dad?

596
00:52:48,311 --> 00:52:50,021
Hey, search the place.

597
00:52:50,105 --> 00:52:50,939
Is he here?

598
00:52:51,022 --> 00:52:52,357
No, sir.

599
00:52:52,440 --> 00:52:53,942
Damn it.

600
00:52:54,567 --> 00:52:56,820
Kid, where did your dad run off to?

601
00:52:57,445 --> 00:52:58,405
I don't know.

602
00:52:58,488 --> 00:53:00,323
"I don't know"?

603
00:53:04,536 --> 00:53:05,495
Damn it.

604
00:53:08,498 --> 00:53:09,708
Come here.

605
00:53:09,791 --> 00:53:11,626
Hold still. I'll be gentle.

606
00:53:11,710 --> 00:53:12,836
Here it is.

607
00:53:13,461 --> 00:53:14,921
Good. This should still work.

608
00:53:15,630 --> 00:53:18,591
Call your dad, kid.

609
00:53:18,675 --> 00:53:19,759
Tell him to come right now.

610
00:53:19,843 --> 00:53:20,719
Here.

611
00:53:21,303 --> 00:53:22,137
That's it.

612
00:53:23,763 --> 00:53:25,056
Jeez.

613
00:53:25,557 --> 00:53:26,725
Give me a cigarette.

614
00:53:30,979 --> 00:53:33,356
Kim is on his way to get you.

615
00:53:33,440 --> 00:53:34,274
Run away now!

616
00:53:38,528 --> 00:53:40,155
Hey, what's taking so long--

617
00:53:40,238 --> 00:53:41,823
Get him!

618
00:54:02,844 --> 00:54:04,512
-Shit.
-Stop right there!

619
00:54:22,530 --> 00:54:24,491
Damn, I'm exhausted.

620
00:54:25,325 --> 00:54:27,535
-We got you now…
-Get him.

621
00:54:28,912 --> 00:54:29,746
Don't lose him.

622
00:54:32,957 --> 00:54:34,542
-Go after him.
-You're so dead.

623
00:55:49,993 --> 00:55:51,286
What are you doing here?

624
00:56:02,839 --> 00:56:04,549
Drink this and dry off before you leave.

625
00:56:05,300 --> 00:56:06,509
You'll catch a cold.

626
00:56:08,011 --> 00:56:09,304
Please.

627
00:56:10,096 --> 00:56:13,850
Be honest with me
and tell me what my problem is.

628
00:56:15,477 --> 00:56:17,520
I'm losing my mind over this.

629
00:56:23,151 --> 00:56:24,777
Everyone just says I'm playing well.

630
00:56:26,779 --> 00:56:28,281
But I know that's not true.

631
00:56:29,699 --> 00:56:32,285
I can't tell if they're clueless
or just pretending to be.

632
00:56:33,828 --> 00:56:35,246
But you know the truth.

633
00:56:36,706 --> 00:56:37,916
Right?

634
00:56:43,880 --> 00:56:45,006
You're right.

635
00:56:46,508 --> 00:56:48,968
I think there's a problem with your music.

636
00:56:50,094 --> 00:56:51,971
Ultimately, your performance

637
00:56:52,722 --> 00:56:54,182
doesn't sound like your own.

638
00:56:55,016 --> 00:56:57,018
Right now, your superb technique

639
00:56:58,061 --> 00:57:00,313
is masking your flaws.

640
00:57:01,231 --> 00:57:03,107
But if you listen closely,

641
00:57:03,816 --> 00:57:06,110
you'll realize that your music is fake.

642
00:57:08,112 --> 00:57:10,448
I admit your technique is flawless.

643
00:57:10,532 --> 00:57:12,659
But music isn't just about technique.

644
00:57:15,620 --> 00:57:18,331
You have to own the emotions
behind that sheet music.

645
00:57:18,414 --> 00:57:20,625
Your pain, your joy, your despair.

646
00:57:21,292 --> 00:57:25,296
Unless you move the audience
with those emotions…

647
00:57:30,802 --> 00:57:32,762
you'll never be a true musician.

648
00:58:05,461 --> 00:58:06,921
Do you have a room available?

649
00:58:07,005 --> 00:58:08,923
We don't accept minors.

650
00:58:09,007 --> 00:58:10,466
Why not?

651
00:58:10,550 --> 00:58:12,010
Come on, I have money.

652
00:58:12,844 --> 00:58:14,012
Just give me a room.

653
00:58:15,930 --> 00:58:16,764
Leave.

654
00:58:32,864 --> 00:58:35,033
DIRECTOR YOON SEON-JU

655
00:58:50,673 --> 00:58:51,674
Hello?

656
00:58:52,300 --> 00:58:54,802
This is Choi Jeong-yo.

657
00:58:57,680 --> 00:58:59,307
Can I stay in the dorm…

658
00:59:01,142 --> 00:59:02,518
for a few days?

659
00:59:32,256 --> 00:59:36,260
Given your situation,
why don't you just transfer to our school?

660
00:59:38,388 --> 00:59:41,307
This isn't pity or charity,
so don't overthink it.

661
00:59:44,227 --> 00:59:48,022
Recruiting smart and talented students

662
00:59:48,106 --> 00:59:49,440
is a huge achievement for me.

663
00:59:50,858 --> 00:59:52,485
And you're a very good candidate.

664
01:00:17,260 --> 01:00:18,803
The phone is turned off.

665
01:00:18,886 --> 01:00:22,890
You will be connected to voicemail
after the beep…

666
01:00:22,974 --> 01:00:24,767
DAD

667
01:00:24,851 --> 01:00:26,686
11:30 P.M.

668
01:00:45,830 --> 01:00:47,290
CHOI JEONG-YO

669
01:01:01,637 --> 01:01:02,472
Attention, everyone.

670
01:01:03,556 --> 01:01:05,308
We have a new transfer student.

671
01:01:06,017 --> 01:01:07,518
Make sure to help him out.

672
01:01:07,602 --> 01:01:08,728
Go ahead and introduce yourself.

673
01:01:16,736 --> 01:01:17,779
Hi, everyone.

674
01:01:17,862 --> 01:01:19,447
Hello.

675
01:01:26,454 --> 01:01:27,789
I see a new face.

676
01:01:28,414 --> 01:01:29,832
-He's a transfer.
-He just transferred.

677
01:01:29,916 --> 01:01:31,083
What's your name?

678
01:01:32,293 --> 01:01:34,378
It's Choi Jeong-yo.

679
01:01:35,421 --> 01:01:36,631
What do you play?

680
01:01:38,424 --> 01:01:39,258
The piano.

681
01:01:39,342 --> 01:01:41,344
Hey, just like you.

682
01:01:41,844 --> 01:01:42,887
Really?

683
01:01:43,888 --> 01:01:44,972
Come to the front.

684
01:01:59,111 --> 01:01:59,946
Play something.

685
01:02:04,075 --> 01:02:06,452
What are you waiting for? Just play.

686
01:02:41,070 --> 01:02:42,196
I…

687
01:02:43,781 --> 01:02:45,199
Can I do it another time?

688
01:02:45,283 --> 01:02:46,534
-What's with him?
-How impressive.

689
01:02:47,368 --> 01:02:48,286
Jeez.

690
01:02:49,704 --> 01:02:50,538
Okay then.

691
01:02:51,414 --> 01:02:52,248
I'm sorry.

692
01:02:57,336 --> 01:02:59,005
All right then.

693
01:02:59,672 --> 01:03:02,800
Let's start at page 139 today.

694
01:03:07,638 --> 01:03:10,057
"Choi Jeong-yo."

695
01:03:11,267 --> 01:03:12,226
How much?

696
01:03:14,228 --> 01:03:15,980
How much did you donate to get in?

697
01:03:17,064 --> 01:03:17,899
Piano, right?

698
01:03:17,982 --> 01:03:20,610
How many? Two or three?

699
01:03:21,110 --> 01:03:22,528
Why won't you tell us?

700
01:03:23,321 --> 01:03:24,280
Hey.

701
01:03:25,573 --> 01:03:28,284
Keep this up, and you're dead.

702
01:03:28,367 --> 01:03:30,036
Gosh, I'm so scared.

703
01:03:32,705 --> 01:03:36,083
Man, you've got no class at all.

704
01:03:37,877 --> 01:03:39,503
It's transfers like him

705
01:03:39,587 --> 01:03:42,048
who drag our school's name
through the mud.

706
01:03:42,131 --> 01:03:45,593
This one brings zero substance

707
01:03:46,302 --> 01:03:47,887
or qualifications.

708
01:03:49,305 --> 01:03:50,181
Move.

709
01:03:52,475 --> 01:03:53,309
What?

710
01:03:53,392 --> 01:03:55,269
I need to get my book, so move.

711
01:03:56,437 --> 01:03:57,855
Make me.

712
01:03:59,398 --> 01:04:00,691
Hey, hey!

713
01:04:00,775 --> 01:04:01,859
What are you boys doing?

714
01:04:02,568 --> 01:04:04,070
You little punks.

715
01:04:04,153 --> 01:04:05,321
Get back in your seats.

716
01:04:20,711 --> 01:04:22,213
Thanks for earlier.

717
01:04:22,296 --> 01:04:23,422
For what?

718
01:04:23,506 --> 01:04:24,966
You stopped them for me.

719
01:04:26,717 --> 01:04:29,470
I didn't stop them.
I was just getting my book.

720
01:04:31,013 --> 01:04:33,099
That's where we sign up
to reserve a practice room?

721
01:04:34,016 --> 01:04:35,309
Where's the snack bar?

722
01:04:35,393 --> 01:04:37,061
You don't live in the dorms, do you?

723
01:04:37,853 --> 01:04:39,939
Why is everything so complicated here?

724
01:04:40,022 --> 01:04:42,233
There are so many classes,
and they're weird.

725
01:04:42,316 --> 01:04:43,192
That's enough.

726
01:04:46,112 --> 01:04:46,946
What is?

727
01:04:47,029 --> 01:04:49,532
I'm not into making friends.

728
01:04:50,866 --> 01:04:51,951
You're on your own.

729
01:05:12,763 --> 01:05:14,348
PRACTICE ROOM RESERVATIONS

730
01:05:50,551 --> 01:05:52,928
Hey, do you have an extra handkerchief?

731
01:06:26,378 --> 01:06:27,671
The grand prize goes to

732
01:06:27,755 --> 01:06:29,757
Choi Jeong-yo!

733
01:06:32,051 --> 01:06:32,968
Have you lost your mind?

734
01:06:33,469 --> 01:06:35,679
How could you place second?

735
01:07:10,089 --> 01:07:12,216
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

736
01:07:12,299 --> 01:07:14,593
You really don't remember me?

737
01:07:14,677 --> 01:07:17,555
There's something I haven't told you.

738
01:07:17,638 --> 01:07:18,764
Just go study abroad.

739
01:07:18,848 --> 01:07:20,933
You think I'd run off
to study abroad like a coward?

740
01:07:21,016 --> 01:07:23,394
How about playing four hands?

741
01:07:23,477 --> 01:07:24,979
I'm sure you know Choi Jeong-yo.

742
01:07:25,062 --> 01:07:27,022
You're using copies
because you can't afford sheet music?

743
01:07:27,106 --> 01:07:28,065
Don't do it!

744
01:07:28,149 --> 01:07:29,650
Why him, of all people?

745
01:07:29,733 --> 01:07:31,277
Have you listened to him play?

746
01:07:31,360 --> 01:07:34,155
I hate bastards like you
who play music with that attitude.

747
01:07:35,281 --> 01:07:38,075
I'm afraid
Choi Jeong-yo will be held accountable.

748
01:07:38,159 --> 01:07:39,743
I'll have him expelled.

749
01:07:40,744 --> 01:07:45,749
Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim

